# Distributor API credentials — TEMPLATE.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is committed and
# must never contain a real value.
#
# How to obtain each credential: docs/sourcing/DISTRIBUTOR-API-SETUP.md
# How to run the pipeline once filled: docs/sourcing/README.md
#
# These are only ever needed LOCALLY. CI reads the committed
# hardware/bom/snapshot.json and never calls a distributor API — a gate that
# queries a live API gives a different answer on every run, so re-retrieval is a
# deliberate act whose result lands in a reviewable diff.

# --- TME (tme.eu) — primary EU distributor, CZ/PL -------------------------
# developers.tme.eu -> API Token keys -> Create application.
# Requests are HMAC-signed: the token is the username, the secret signs the
# request. Market data additionally needs the header `request-context: anonymous`.
TME_TOKEN=
TME_APP_SECRET=

# --- Mouser EU (mouser.de — DE warehouse) --------------------------------
# Complete the Search API Request Form; the key arrives by email.
# Free tier: 1,000 requests/day, 30/minute.
MOUSER_SEARCH_API_KEY=

# --- Digi-Key EU (digikey.de — NL warehouse) -----------------------------
# developer.digikey.com -> Organization -> Production Apps -> Create Production App.
# OAuth 2.0 two-legged: exchange these for a short-lived bearer token.
# Free tier: 1,000 requests/day, 120/minute.
DIGIKEY_CLIENT_ID=
DIGIKEY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Which Digi-Key host to call. Start on the sandbox: the flow is identical and
# it does not spend production quota, which is what you want while the per-vendor
# field mapping is still being written against a recorded response.
#   sandbox-api.digikey.com   <- start here
#   api.digikey.com           <- once the mapping is proven
DIGIKEY_API_HOST=sandbox-api.digikey.com
